# Capacitor build: `npm run build:mobile`
#
# The native app has no "own origin" — it loads from capacitor:// or the
# filesystem — so the relative URLs the web build uses cannot resolve. Point it
# at the deployed nginx instead, which serves both halves.
#
# Vite precedence puts .env.mobile above .env.local, so this overrides local dev
# values without touching them.
#
# CORS matters here and only here. The web build is same-origin, so it never
# sends a preflight; the Capacitor app is the one cross-origin client, calling
# from capacitor://localhost (iOS) or http://localhost (Android). nginx does not
# emit CORS headers — it forwards the OPTIONS like any other method and the
# backend's CORSMiddleware answers, so ALLOWED_ORIGINS must contain both.
VITE_API_URL=https://CHANGE-ME.example.com/api
VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://CHANGE-ME.example.com
